      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14250342/assets/952f35d03c8554f2feaeb50296df9ac426a49730a44038bf6f9cf47b1fa3f9ee.png)\n\nThe vector $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\frac{5}{2}.$ Find the vector $Av.$",
      "worked_solution": "The eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\frac{5}{2}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14250342/assets/cb3fae2e42e90e7e8398c311fd9c4d20ac1db51687a7d4f3f77146eb53728de5.png)",
